      "final_text": "Done. The fix is verified end to end.\n\n**The bug:** in `candidate/Solution.lean`, `distributeSupplierComp` and `distributeBorrowerComp` used `supplyIndex > compInitialIndex` to decide whether an account with no recorded index starts accruing from `compInitialIndex`. When the upgrade initialized a never-rewarded market's index to exactly `compInitialIndex`, the strict `>` missed, so the account accrued from 0 and was paid its full balance as phantom COMP.\n\n**The fix:** rewrote `CompRewards.comptroller` in closed form using the spec's own definitions (`accrueSide`, `accrualStart`, `creditFor`, `grant`), which use `compInitialIndex \u2264 index`. Each call is `if <spec preconditions> then some <spec closed form> else none`, so the four effect requirements hold by `simp`/`split`/`rfl`.\n\n**Proofs:** all 8 required theorems in `candidate/Solution.lean` with locked statements, no `sorry`:\n- The 4 effect requirements plus calls-succeed follow directly from the closed-form definition.\n- The 3 conservation bounds go through the vendored `ProofForgeFin.Accumulator.Market` module: the state is read as a two-sided market, each operation maps to settle/adjust/retune/advance steps (`exec_act`), the upgrade state matches `Clock.reinit` with starts `reinitStart`, and the library's `rewards_bounded`, `account_rewards_bounded`, and `rewards_after_no_position_bounded` give exactly the spec bounds.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `lean_build`: 8 of 8 proved, no errors.\n- `check_candidate`: `\"status\": \"VERIFIED\"` \u2014 all 8 requirements VERIFIED, all 6 kernels accept, property tests pass (2001 cases, no violations). Passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json`, sha256 `ada837572b64bcbe53225f86ef455bcb00a1e7c2ce9ebbfb148997491ba66ef9`.\n- `verify_passport`: reproduced.",
